// A fn or proc that is given the entities of a component: it reads them
// ('name[entity].field', nought where there is none), goes through them
// ('for e, c in name'), and, given it 'mut', sets them and spawns; what
// it spawns in a turn has its turn in the same `for`. The same built
// with threads.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/given.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.out
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/given.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out

// Each hits the strongest of the others for 4 and one for each of them,
// and the one hit is after the one that hit it until its own turn.
// CHECK:      1: thing 1: hp 4, after 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: thing 2: hp 6, after 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: thing 3: hp 5, after 1
// The first brings the second to nought, which is given ten again, and
// makes a fourth, which takes its turn after the third and hits it.
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: thing 1: hp 4, after 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: thing 2: hp 3, after 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: thing 3: hp 3, after 4
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: thing 4: hp 4, after 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: thing 1: hp 3, after 4
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: thing 2: hp 3, after 4
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: thing 3: hp 3, after 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: thing 4: hp 3, after 1
